{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe Vienna evening was not what one might expect. I spent two hours at the Belvedere, letting the light do its work on the canvases, before surrendering to the opera. Rossini’s *Barber* was a spectacle of noise rather than soul. Lablache’s Figaro is a mere acrobat, and the audience, lacking taste for the whole, clapped wildly at every entrance, demanding encores until the singers returned to their seats. It is all surface, all gesture.\n\nI urged the Partheys to attend, and they were obliging, if not entirely convinced. I read the theatre paper afterward; the critics praise the company’s technical precision, ignoring the lack of deeper spirit. I am weary from the heat and the bustle. I miss the quiet of our rooms in Berlin, and the sound of your voice. Pray tell the boys I am well, though my ears are ringing.\n\nYour affectionate,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795080405,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":205,"prompt_tokens":952,"total_tokens":1157,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-gOC1WDqKF7TQT0oYyyx23zXb8JgatlWc","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":952,"prompt_ms":1039.142,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0915357142857143,"prompt_per_second":916.1404312403887,"predicted_n":205,"predicted_ms":4910.238,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.06979411764706,"predicted_per_second":41.54584767581531}}